(6666418, 994701, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>The title of your image made me laugh because my bf, <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=108544" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Magnumphotography</a>, fits that descrip to a T, check out his profile and you''ll see :-)<br/> <br/>I do like the sense of depth that the flower gives but its shape doesn''t automatically register as a flower; it may have been better to put the spider by itself on the tabletop, or even on a miniature set of some sort, have some fun with it.  The greyish b/g is amorphous and tends to compete with the light colour of the flower for the eye.  The spider itself looks quite colourful and friendly but yeah, spiders and bugs generally don''t get much of a fair shake here...unless you''re <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=67145" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">roz</a>, also an Aussie.  She''s brilliant at macros and can definitely give you some pointers.  I like the eye-level POV, it''s a bit unsettling.  Which is probably why I like it!<br/> <br/>Overall not a bad finish at all for one of your first entries.  Get Mr Spider out and have some fun shooting him/her in different areas, different focal lengths.  Experiment and have fun and by all means keep entering imges that you like.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me,<br/> <br/>Susan<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! The title of your image made me laugh because my bf,  Magnumphotography, fits that descrip to a T, check out his profile and you''ll see :-) I do like the sense of depth that the flower gives but its shape doesn''t automatically register as a flower; it may have been better to put the spider by itself on the tabletop, or even on a miniature set of some sort, have some fun with it.  The greyish b/g is amorphous and tends to compete with the light colour of the flower for the eye.  The spider itself looks quite colourful and friendly but yeah, spiders and bugs generally don''t get much of a fair shake here...unless you''re  roz, also an Aussie.  She''s brilliant at macros and can definitely give you some pointers.  I like the eye-level POV, it''s a bit unsettling.  Which is probably why I like it! Overall not a bad finish at all for one of your first entries.  Get Mr Spider out and have some fun shooting him/her in different areas, different focal lengths.  Experiment and have fun and by all means keep entering imges that you like. Feel free to PM me, Susan ', '2012-02-07 17:16:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(6667136, 994618, 12611, '<td valign="top">Only you could pick up ordinary objects, shoot it process it and slap a great title on it, and end up with a classic shot. I feel the abstract qualities, and the sunrise with remarkably true colors... voters be damned!</td>', 'Only you could pick up ordinary objects, shoot it process it and slap a great title on it, and end up with a classic shot. I feel the abstract qualities, and the sunrise with remarkably true colors... voters be damned!', '2012-02-08 08:31:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(6667505, 994583, 134859, '<td valign="top">White balance does seem a little off... however, I disagree with the other comments... I think that with the shavings being the only thing in focus, it makes for a very interesting picture.  <br/> <br/>Then again, I like "different" pictures... <br/> <br/>If the white balance was there, it is an image I could see hanging in my children''s room.  Honestly.  Good work.</td>', 'White balance does seem a little off... however, I disagree with the other comments... I think that with the shavings being the only thing in focus, it makes for a very interesting picture.   Then again, I like "different" pictures...  If the white balance was there, it is an image I could see hanging in my children''s room.  Honestly.  Good work.', '2012-02-08 15:51:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(6678113, 994884, 134859, '<td valign="top">I''m one of the few who gave you a 7 on this.  I really liked it.  The bright colors, the darkness, even the shadow on the wall.</td>', 'I''m one of the few who gave you a 7 on this.  I really liked it.  The bright colors, the darkness, even the shadow on the wall.', '2012-02-15 15:27:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(6678297, 994097, 133853, '<td valign="top">It''s definitely macro... F16 and 6 second exposure! :) I could have just used one of the beans with quite amazing detail, but that wasn''t my idea....<br/> <br/>If you have any macro tips for me Michel I would appreciate them, as I do find it very difficult. :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-02-15 17:57:24.</i></td>', 'It''s definitely macro... F16 and 6 second exposure! :) I could have just used one of the beans with quite amazing detail, but that wasn''t my idea.... If you have any macro tips for me Michel I would appreciate them, as I do find it very difficult. :)', '2012-02-15 17:54:04.000000', '2012-02-15 17:57:24.000000', 0),
